# 🗺️ G5S | Spatial Conflict Analysis & Locational Criteria Platform

An interactive **R Shiny** Web Application engineered for automated spatial conflict screening, locational criteria assessment, and preliminary environmental licensing reports in the State of Minas Gerais, Brazil.

Developed for **G5S Projetos e Consultoria Ambiental**, the system dynamically interfaces with official state spatial data infrastructures via the **Web Feature Service (WFS)** protocol to evaluate geographic constraints under **DN COPAM n.º 217/2017**.

---

## 🌟 Key Features

* **Real-time WFS Integration:** Connects directly to the GeoServer of the State System for Environment and Water Resources (**IDE-SISEMA**), consuming live spatial feature layers without local database clutter.
* **Flexible Spatial Input Methods:**
  * **File Upload:** Import enterprise boundaries directly via Shapefile (.zip), KML, or GeoJSON.
  * **Manual Coordinates:** Generate buffered Area of Direct Influence (ADA) polygons instantly from decimal coordinates and customized radiuses.
  * **Interactive On-Screen Drawing:** Trace custom polygon geometries directly on top of satellite and topographic basemaps.
* **Automated DN COPAM 217/2017 Batch Filter:** Single-click feature selector pre-filters critical regulatory layers (Conservation Units, Buffer Zones, APPs, Ramsar Sites, Cavity Potential, Water Conflict Areas, etc.).
* **Spatial Intersection Engine:**
  * Computes geometric intersections using `sf` in UTM projection (SIRGAS 2000 / UTM 23S - EPSG:31983).
  * Evaluates specific attribute criteria (e.g., Cavity Potential grades, Water Body Framing).
* **Interactive Conflict Visualization:** Displays intersected spatial features on a dedicated Leaflet map with rich attribute popups and geometry group controls.
* **Automated Technical Report Generator:** Compiles spatial screening findings into a preliminary legal report (HTML/PDF ready to print) and structured Excel workbooks (.xlsx).
* **Vector Conflict Package Export:** Downloads all intercepted official geometries as ready-to-use Shapefile archives (.zip).
* **Resource Security Management:** Features an automated 5-minute client inactivity session timeout to optimize server performance.

---

## 📜 Regulatory & Legal Framework

The platform evaluates locational weights and spatial prohibitions according to **Deliberação Normativa COPAM n.º 217/2017** (Tables 4 and 5):

* **Weight 2 Criteria:** Full Protection Conservation Units, Extreme/Special Priority Vegetation Suppression Areas, Ramsar Sites.
* **Weight 1 Criteria:** Native Vegetation Suppression, Buffer Zones (3 km radius), Sustainable Use Conservation Units, Biosphere Reserves, Ecological Corridors, Water Conflict Areas, High/Very High Cavity Potential.
* **Severe Restrictions & Prohibitions:** Permanent Preservation Areas (APP - State Law 20.922/2013), Atlantic Forest Biosphere (Federal Law 11.428/2006), Airport Security Areas (ASA), Special Class Water Bodies.

